WEBVTT

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:14.860
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.070
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.990
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:43.870
<b>Chapter Two               Azure Encounter</b>

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.690
Hot... So hot.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:01.280
Saying that it's hot will not,

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.280
in fact, make it cooler.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.500
Nishinosono-san, we're going camping, right?

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.060
Yes, I can't wait.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.820
Is this your car?

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:12.680
Yes.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.410
Wow...

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.650
Wait, where's your luggage?

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.570
It'll be here in a second.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.300
Hello.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.670
I am Suwano, the lady's butler.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:41.250
Please take good care of her.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.880
He said he was a butler.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.320
What's a butler?

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.310
I'll explain later, Wu-san.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.830
I'll take a picture...

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:50.970
Fuchida-san!

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.000
Everyone.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.650
Yes?

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.780
Could you help me unload my luggage?

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:57.700
Sure.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.280
Thank you very much.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.420
Sensei?

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.650
Please take good care of the lady.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.040
All right.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.330
It'll be fine. Leave her to me.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:15.600
She was so looking forward to this.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.080
Even I can tell she's happy.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:24.080
Even more because you'll be accompanying her.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.640
To put it in terms she might use,

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.730
her happiness has increased exponentially.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.860
Nishinosono-san, this is too heavy!

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.530
What are you bringing?

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.110
Ice cream.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.260
Ice cream? On a camping trip?

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.870
Everything you do is like something out of a fairytale...

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.410
What's a fairytale?

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.450
I'll tell you later.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.350
Thank you so much, everyone—

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.420
You help, too!

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:52.340
And since her parents are no longer with us,

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:56.760
she gets few opportunities like this.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.490
Here.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.220
I brought a dessert just for you!

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.820
Is that supposed to be a joke?

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.100
Um, you're Saikawa-sensei, yes?

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.160
Yes.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:20.480
<b>Vice Director    Yamane Yukihiro</b>

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.480
My name is Yamane Yukihiro. 
I'm with the Magata Laboratory.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.280
The director has asked me

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.950
to show you around.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.000
I see.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.180
You're dressed rather casually.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:32.370
Basically, the only rule around 
here is that there are no rules.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.500
<b>School of Engineering, Architectural Department 
Assistant Professor 

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.500
I'm Saikawa. Thank you for having us.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.590
I hope this camping trip isn't 
causing trouble for you.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.440
Not at all.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.270
We've never had so many guests before.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.610
Thank you.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.360
Nishinosono-kun,

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.420
this is Yamane-san, the facility's vice director.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.520
Nice to meet you. I'm Nishinosono.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.220
I've never met you in person,

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.900
but I did watch the recording of 
your meeting with Dr. Magata.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.470
That was being recorded?

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.300
I thought it was private...

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.470
It was quite an interesting conversation.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.160
Excuse me.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.670
As a matter of course, meetings with 
Dr. Magata are made public.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.310
I will say that everyone was extremely jealous.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:32.060
I've been at the lab for fifteen years,

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.190
and I've never had the chance to speak 
with her about anything but work.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:40.810
And all those discussions occurred 
with a mike and camera.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.080
Does the doctor never meet with anyone?

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:45.070
No.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.760
After what happened,

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.600
it would be more accurate to 
say that she's kept isolated.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.830
For the past fifteen years, Dr. Magata hasn't

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.450
taken a single step outside.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:05.830
Well, she's been conducting a lot of 
interviews via computer lately.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:10.130
But her conversation with you 
was the first of its kind.

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:13.150
You're a lucky girl, aren't you, Nishinosono-kun?

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.720
You look jealous, Sensei.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:21.190
Saikawa-sensei is a huge, huge, 
huge fan of Dr. Magata's!

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.210
Yamane-san,

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.480
how many times per day does 
this boat arrive at the island?

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.300
Oh, it doesn't make regular trips.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.200
Normally, this ship doesn't go to Himaka Island.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.680
It goes to Shino Island, which is past Himaka.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:37.190
During that trip, we simply have it stop

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.340
at our island.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.770
And we have to call for it to come.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.270
Then how does the lab's network function?

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:49.120
It's protected.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.530
It's completely isolated from the outside world,

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:56.170
and it's impossible to privately 
communicate with Dr. Magata.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:58.810
You're trying to keep your secrets from leaking?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.270
Of course that's part of it.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.540
But the most important thing is that

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.280
Dr. Magata can only be contacted

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.510
if the conversation is recorded and 
monitored by multiple people.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:14.490
Magata Shiki's talent is

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.150
our lab's most important asset.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:21.860
So she herself is the main system, yes?

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:23.670
Exactly.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.920
<b>No Signal</b>

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:28.330
And naturally, there are no cell towers, 
since they're unnecessary...

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:32.420
Truly an ideal environment.

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.340
Doctor,

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.040
you've been in that room for 
fifteen years, haven't you?

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:43.720
In an environment with no seasons, day, or night.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.690
What has changed?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.840
I shall start by saying that

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:54.620
I did not come here of my own free will.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.700
But many things inside me have 
taken on lives of their own.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:03.080
You could say, in a sense, that has stabilized me,

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.830
anchoring me in reality.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:09.200
Do you not need any type of physical access?

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.180
Reality affects us all, regardless of our wishes.

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:16.620
From an energy standpoint, it's more efficient

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:20.100
to limit physical access to the 
maximum degree possible.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.660
In the future, physically meeting 
someone, in the real world,

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:26.910
will become a luxury, like jewelry.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:31.320
Even shaking another's hand will come 
to constitute a special occasion.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.870
Which means

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:36.070
you won't be able to kill another person.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.200
A brilliant insight.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.350
Here, Nishinosono-san.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:50.460
Hamanaka...

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.530
Don't spoil her.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:55.280
She hasn't done a thing!

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:58.490
Sorry, I've never held a knife in my life,

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.470
so I don't know how to use one.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.470
You don't know how to use a knife?

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.380
This is delicious!

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.600
Who did the flavoring?

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.110
I just put some yakiniku sauce on it.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.440
Who made that sauce?

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:15.090
Listen... I bought it in a store.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:21.060
Is that yakisoba?

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.790
I've always wanted to try that!

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.710
You've never had yakisoba?

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.070
Kawabata...

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:30.210
Later.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:42.980
Is that the helicopter that was at the lab?

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.570
Wow, look at all the stars!

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.990
I can't believe she's lived the last fifteen years

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.220
without seeing a beautiful sky like this!

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:02.060
But that way of life is beautiful, as well.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.730
Seeing nature and thinking it's 
beautiful is what's unnatural.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.090
That means the life you lead is an unclean one.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.460
You think so?

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:19.090
If you can cut yourself off from 
Mother Nature and still survive,

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.060
doesn't it mean you have enough 
inner beauty to allow you to do that?

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.870
You're thinking about Dr. Magata, aren't you?

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:33.280
Sensei, can I have a smoke?

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:34.980
You're still a minor, right?

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:36.830
I'm almost twenty.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.990
I'm going to the lab now.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.870
Right now? Alone?

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:46.450
Actually, I've already scheduled 
it with someone from the lab.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:50.200
Wait, why didn't you tell me 
something so important?

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:53.900
This is more important to you than 
our camping trip, isn't it?

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:55.630
No, that isn't what I meant.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.090
Then what did you mean?

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:00.190
Anyway, it's dark and dangerous.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.210
If you're going, I'll go with you.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.630
Okay.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:08.400
But in exchange, when we get back, 
you're going on a date with me.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:12.750
I don't know if you should be involving 
others in these negotiations.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:20.860
Sensei, are you just keeping me around, 
even though you don't like me?

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.840
Is it because I'm Nishinosono Kyosuke's daughter?

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.620
Listen, Nishinosono-kun.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:38.860
Outside of work hours, I never 
do anything I don't want to.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.990
And right now, we're outside of work hours.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:51.000
Dr. Magata really is on this island, isn't she?

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.790
That's right. I met her.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.360
What should I do?

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.790
Should I get her autograph?

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.900
I'm sorry, Uncle.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.400
Wanting to leave so suddenly this way is selfish.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.490
No, I don't mind.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.890
I want to see the ocean.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:10.700
You've seen the ocean.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.780
I've never seen it at night.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.070
All right.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.180
We'll go to the yacht harbor nearby.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:19.630
There's also a bowling alley and an arcade, too.

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.530
You think of me as a child, don't you?

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:26.180
Yes, you're still a child, you know.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:28.890
Sensei...

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:31.870
Oh, sorry.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.210
I want to see the ocean!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.240
You can see it... It's right over—

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.360
Come on!

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.320
When we get there, I want to see a lighthouse.

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:44.640
And a tunnel, too. And limestone caves.

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.630
And I want to look at a railway bridge from below.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:49.640
And then...

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:51.750
We don't have time for all of those.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.750
No, I want to see all of them.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.940
I want to go into the sea at night.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:58.700
And then I want to drink with you, Sensei.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:00.150
But you're still a minor—

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:01.260
Be quiet, please!

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.300
And then I want to try alcohol.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:07.750
Shiki, you're still thirteen.

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.050
Then I can't?

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.270
Of course not.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:16.770
This is the worst.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.160
Instead of going camping,

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.650
I really want to go on a trip, just you and me.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.090
Nishinosono-kun...

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:28.030
Back there, were you drinking beer?

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:30.590
This is the worst!

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:32.020
Enough of this!

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:34.160
It's dangerous to walk that fast.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.330
What did you tell your wife about tonight?

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:41.570
That a friend's father died, and I was 
attending the memorial service.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.670
Liar.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.310
I don't exactly have a choice, do I?

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.680
And what did your wife say?

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.640
She won't be home tonight.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.400
She's staying over somewhere.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.430
Then I don't have to go back...

00:13:58.210 --> 00:13:59.440
What you're doing is dangerous.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:01.570
I know.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.150
<i>Are you part of the staff?</i>

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:13.660
No.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.080
<i>Please wait a moment.</i>

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.120
Yes, who's there?

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:25.420
Hello, I'm Nishinosono, from Nagono University.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.500
I'd like to speak to Yamane-san.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:28.700
What's wrong?

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:31.740
I have a terrible headache...

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:35.060
I was hoping I could get some medicine.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.220
All right, just a moment.

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.070
Are you okay, Nishinosono-san?

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:49.160
It gets really bad sometimes...

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:52.580
If I can get some medicine, I think it'll get better.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.960
For now, just come inside.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:55.080
Thank you...

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.140
Yamane Yukihiro.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.680
Put your right hand here, and say your name.

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:04.400
All right.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.790
Saikawa Sohei.

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.650
Nishinosono Moe.

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:14.390
<i>Two persons registered as guests.</i>

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:17.700
Deborah, send a message to any staff still awake,

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:21.900
asking anyone with headache medicine 
to bring it to the lobby.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.280
<i>Understood.</i>

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:26.430
Um, who is Deborah?

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:28.490
The name of one of the subsystems.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:32.240
Deborah does that, as well.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.010
Can I smoke in here?

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:40.410
Yeah, you can smoke almost anywhere in the lab.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.250
These days, that's rare.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.750
Aren't you happy, Sensei?

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:49.150
Oh, Yamane-san, a while ago, 
didn't I hear a helicopter?

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:52.110
Yes. That was the director leaving.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.300
Where's he going at this hour?

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.200
Oh, well...

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:59.340
Huh? Nishinosono-san, are you feeling better?

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:01.160
Yes...

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:05.480
A little bit, but I'd still like some medicine...

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:16.790
Deborah, send P1 back.

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:18.800
Wow, that's amazing!

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.120
What's P1?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.080
The name of this cart.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:40.060
Would you like to rest in my room a while?

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:41.630
Yes!

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:45.080
Please...

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:47.900
Hot!

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:53.040
Nishinosono-san, you came 
to see Dr. Magata, didn't you?

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.860
O-Oh, no...

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.330
I'm sorry we tried to trick you.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:01.650
No, I tricked Sensei and brought him here.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:02.890
I'm sorry.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:07.070
Well, I was getting a little bored,

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:08.810
so it's no bother.

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:11.020
Thank you.

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.320
And so, the doctor...

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:14.800
Well...

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:17.600
We keep calling her, without response.

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:20.430
Could she have collapsed inside her room?

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:22.580
It's possible,

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:26.010
but with the director gone, 
we can't just barge in there—

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.050
No! We should go inside!

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:30.190
Her life might be in danger!

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:34.570
But... The door to the doctor's room is locked.

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:36.110
What do you mean?

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:39.360
My guess is that it's software trouble.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:43.660
In the worst case, we can break down the door...

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:47.960
But I don't think we can do that 
without the director here.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.950
Where did the director go?

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:53.860
He went to get Dr. Magata's younger sister.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:56.180
Dr. Magata has a younger sister?

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:59.280
Yes, though that's not public knowledge...

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:01.630
Just a moment.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:05.290
What is it?

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:07.600
Yamane-san, we're back on-line.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.260
What was the cause?

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:11.590
No clue. It just suddenly came back.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.530
Got it. I'll head straight over.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.000
The door might open.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.450
Will you come with me?

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.920
Yes, I'd like to.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.870
Yamane Yukihiro.

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:34.100
This is Saikawa-sensei and Nishinosono-san, 
from Nagono University.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:38.270
This is Mizutani-kun and Shimada-san. 
They work here.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.160
That's the door.

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:44.810
You're really opening it?

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:49.220
For fifteen years, no one's opened it 
without the doctor's permission.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:53.660
Make the call, Yamane-san.

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:55.860
You're in charge right now, aren't you?

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:00.990
Let's open it.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:02.830
Are you sure? She's a murderer.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:05.690
She's fine now.

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:07.050
Don't make assumptions!

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:09.790
We, the security personnel, will take 
the fall if something happens!

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:11.430
What happened?

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:13.050
What's going on here?

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:15.460
Mochizuki-san, the door is opening!

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.850
Deborah, check the lights.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:22.470
<i>Irregularity detected.</i>

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:23.600
Did someone open the door?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.510
I didn't do it! It opened on its own!

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:38.360
Who's there?

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:48.660
A doll?

00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:02.430
P1?

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:13.520
That isn't a doll! It's Dr. Magata!

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:14.770
Someone, stop it!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.460
Deborah, shut down all P1's!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.870
<i>That command cannot be executed now.</i>

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:21.080
Reset!

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.280
<i>A normal reset cannot be executed now.</i>

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.660
<i>Will you execute an emergency reset?</i>

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:26.660
Reset!

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.500
<i>Command recognized.</i>

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.370
<i>All functions will shut down for one minute.</i>

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:38.010
<i>There were too many people</i>

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:41.490
<i>around her who treated her like a genius.</i>

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:46.550
<i>But to me, she was just a thirteen-year-old girl.</i>

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:50.410
<i>No, I had thought of her as a girl, but...</i>

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:52.880
<i>Whenever I was alone with her,</i>

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:56.150
<i>there was always a slight sense of terror.</i>

00:20:56.660 --> 00:21:00.010
<i>She ruled my life.</i>

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:01.360
<i>She toyed with it.</i>

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:03.860
<i>Or perhaps, I wanted her to rule it</i>

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:05.360
<i>and to toy with it.</i>

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.780
<i>I wanted to touch her, 
and my hands moved slightly.</i>

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:13.160
<i>She always anticipated this moment's hesitation.</i>

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:16.310
<i>Part of me realized that</i>

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:19.900
<i>this terror was an expression of</i>

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:22.130
<i>another, different feeling.</i>

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.540
<i>Or so I'd thought...</i>
